{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Woe to those who rise early.</b> [It is in] construct state even though what follows [is governed] by bet, and like it: \"those who dwell in tents\" (Judges 8:11)." "And likewise <b>who tarry late at neshef</b> [means] the beginning of the night, and likewise: \"at neshef, in the evening of the day\" (Proverbs 7:9). \"The stars of its neshef\" (Job 3:9), for neshef is sometimes adjacent to the morning." "And the word <b>they kindle them</b> is conjugated for two [object] particles, from the root of \"for you burned after\" (Genesis 31:36). And some say [it is] from the Aramaic translation: they kindle them in Aramaic."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:27.122364759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}